cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or code, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Red-flag Research: live, public screening for automated-research attacks on peer review"
abstract: >-
  Benchmark release of a research project that screens conference submissions
  for passages, numbers or tables that closely match an earlier public paper
  without clear attribution: an anonymized diagnostic set of ICLR 2027 target
  papers with candidate sources, evidence locations, human labels, saved
  baseline outputs and evaluation tools.
authors:
  - name: "OpenLAIR"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OpenLAIR/red-flag-research"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - source attribution
  - research integrity
  - scientific papers
  - benchmark
  - language models
